{{also|frog-march|frog march}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|frog march}}
* {{l|en|frog-march}}
* {{l|en|frog's march}}

===Etymology===
See {{m|en|frog march}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To march or force a person forward while holding their arms from behind or the side, as a prisoner.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To force a person forward against their will.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1940|author={{w|Thomas Firbank}}|title=I Bought a Mountain| passage=The wind '''frogmarched''' me at a run into the house.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} To carry a person [[face-down]] with one person holding each limb.
# To [[forcibly]] [[relocate]] a person, especially in a [[degrading]] or [[humiliating]] manner.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The process of frogmarching a person.

